  "question": {
    "html": "<p>The graph shows how the pressure of an ideal gas in a sealed container of volume <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"V\"></span> varies with temperature. The number of gas molecules in the container is <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"A\"></span>. </p>\n\n<figure data-asset-id=\"fig_01\"><img alt=\"Source question diagram 1\" src=\"asset:fig_01\"/></figure>\n\n<p>What is the gradient of the graph?</p>\n<p></p>\n<ol class=\"mcq-options\">\n<li data-label=\"A\"><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"\\frac{AR}{V}\"></span></li>\n<li data-label=\"B\"><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"\\frac{A}{VR}\"></span></li>\n<li data-label=\"C\"><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"\\frac{Ak_{B}}{V}\"></span></li>\n<li data-label=\"D\"><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"\\frac{A}{k_{B}V}\"></span></li>\n</ol>"
